coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder identities create [flags] [name]

  Create a delegated identity under you

  Creating an identity returns a record and no credential. The identity gets its
  credentials where it is used: in a workspace created on its behalf.

OPTIONS:
  -c, --column [name|parent|root user|scopes|effective scopes|created at|id] (default: name,parent,root user,scopes,effective scopes)
          Columns to display in table output.

      --org string
          The organization of the identity, when its parent is in more than one.

  -o, --output table|json (default: table)
          Output format.

      --parent string
          The delegated identity or user to create the identity under. It
          defaults to you.

      --scope string-array
          A scope the identity may use with the Coder API, as API tokens name
          them. Repeat for more. Without any, the identity can do nothing.

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
